Colour palettes
  Gruvbox Material, https://github.com/sainnhe/gruvbox-material, MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 sainnhe.
  Gruvbox, https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox, declared MIT/X11 (its repository has no LICENSE file).
  Their colour values are used across the colour files (terminals, btop, eza, lazygit, zellij, yazi
  and niri settings). Only the colour values are used.

btop theme (Apache-2.0)
  config/btop/themes/dotfiles-gruvbox-material-dark.theme is adapted from, and changed against, btop's bundled
  gruvbox_material_dark theme (btop, https://github.com/aristocratos/btop, Apache-2.0). The colour roles were
  re-mapped. Licence text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

niri default configuration (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  niri, https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri. These files reproduce comments, values and bind lines from niri's
  default-config.kdl and are therefore GPL-3.0-or-later (see their SPDX headers):
    config/niri/config.example.kdl
    config/niri/dotfiles.d/31-layout.kdl
    config/niri/dotfiles.d/40-binds-navigation.kdl
    config/niri/dotfiles.d/50-window-rules.kdl
  The other niri fragments are original and MIT. Licence text: LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt.

Yazi
  config/fish/functions/y.fish is adapted from the shell wrapper in the Yazi documentation
  (https://yazi-rs.github.io, Yazi is MIT).

Not shipped (install them from their own sources, under their own licences)
  Papirus icon theme (GPL-3.0); GTK, libadwaita and GNOME Shell themes (see the gnome-themes repo);
  GNOME Shell extensions (Dash to Dock, Forge, User Themes and others); yazi plugins and the yazi
  gruvbox-material flavor; the fonts named in the configs (JetBrains Mono and Adwaita Mono Nerd Fonts).
